{{!
    @template tool_quicktranslate/sidebar_items

    The rows of the quick translate sidebar, one per string the page resolved.

    Rendered on the client when the panel is first opened, from the json the sidebar shipped, so a
    page resolving a thousand strings does not put a thousand rows in the document unasked. A
    template of its own so this markup is not built by hand in javascript.

    Classes required for JS:
    * quicktranslate-item
    * translate - the value currently shown on the page, read back when reporting a save

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-id - string reference as identifier/component

    Context variables required for this template:
    * langstrings - list of {identifier, component, text}

    Example context (json):
    {
        "langstrings": [
            {"identifier": "yes", "component": "core", "text": "Yes"},
            {"identifier": "pluginname", "component": "mod_forum", "text": "Forum"}
        ]
    }
}}
{{#langstrings}}
    <li class="list-group-item p-0">
        <button type="button" class="quicktranslate-item btn btn-link text-start w-100 px-3 py-2"
                data-id="{{identifier}}/{{component}}">
            <span class="identifier fst-italic d-block">{{identifier}}/{{component}}</span>
            <span class="translate">{{text}}</span>
        </button>
    </li>
{{/langstrings}}
